{"kind":"project","sections":[{"projectFiles":"OUDS-Onboarding-Tutorial.zip","xcodeRequirement":"Xcode 27.1","kind":"hero","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Let’s suppose we want to define a view for corporate apps with headings, texts, buttons and images.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"How can we do that?","type":"text"}]}],"title":"Define information cards","backgroundImage":"ic_theme_intro.png","chapter":"Define information cards","estimatedTimeInMinutes":45,"image":"ic_theme_intro.png"},{"kind":"tasks","tasks":[{"contentSection":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Before designing awesome SwiftUI view with OUDS, we need to write before the properties of such view."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"You should have an access to "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/www.figma.com\/design\/zJl6GhY2gMSMAibBJXoNPy\/Reveal-and-Onboarding?node-id=2259-4970&m=dev"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"kind":"contentAndMedia","mediaPosition":"trailing"}],"anchor":"Define-the-view-basics","title":"Define the view basics","stepsSection":[{"type":"step","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Define a basic "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"InfoCard"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View"},{"type":"text","text":", it must have an asset name to load as image, a title, a subtitle, a description and a label for the button."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Add also the Xcode "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#Preview"},{"type":"text","text":" macro to display the view, here of course it will be empty."}]}],"media":null,"code":"tutorial-onboarding-2-1.swift","runtimePreview":"tutorial-onboarding-2-1.png","caption":[]},{"type":"step","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDS library provides view modifiers to be used in Xcode previews macros."},{"type":"text","text"